---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Self-hostable, serverless RSS for the web and native clients">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">✦ serverless · self-hostable · open</p>
      <h1>Your feeds, yours.<br /><span class="accent">No server to babysit.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Sparkle RSS is a self-hostable RSS / Atom reader rebuilt from scratch as a fully
        serverless AWS application. It drops straight into NetNewsWire, Reeder, Capy,
        Vienna, and every other Google Reader–compatible client — and ships with a calm,
        keyboard-first web reader of its own.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-lg" href="/setup">self-host it</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://app.sparklerss.com">open the live app</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="hero-stats">
        <li><span class="stat-num">$0</span> idle monthly server cost</li>
        <li><span class="stat-num">≈$12</span> worst-case monthly, total</li>
        <li><span class="stat-num">TypeScript</span> end to end</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="features" class="features">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">features</p>
      <h2>Everything you expect from a reader.<br />None of the upkeep.</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="chip">sync</span>
          <h3>Drop-in for native clients</h3>
          <p>
            Full wire-level compatibility with the Google Reader API that NetNewsWire and
            friends speak natively. Point any compatible app at your server and it just works.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="chip">web</span>
          <h3>A reader that respects your attention</h3>
          <p>
            Terminal-inspired, typography-first, keyboard-driven. Collapsible sidebar,
            infinite scroll, virtualized lists, dark and light schemes.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="chip">serverless</span>
          <h3>AWS, no servers to patch</h3>
          <p>
            Aurora DSQL, Lambda, CloudFront, Cognito. Near-zero cost when idle, auto-scales
            when you catch up after a week away. Nothing to SSH into.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="chip">open</span>
          <h3>Yours, reproducibly</h3>
          <p>
            Everything is defined in Terraform. Deploy the exact same stack from a clean
            checkout — no undocumented manual steps, no long-lived cloud keys.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="architecture" class="architecture">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">architecture</p>
      <h2>A fully serverless pipeline</h2>
      <ol class="arch-list">
        <li>
          <span class="arch-idx">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Ingestion</h3>
            <p>
              An EventBridge scheduler wakes every five minutes, fans subscriptions out to
              Lambda workers, and refreshes feeds with conditional GETs and per-feed error
              backoff.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="arch-idx">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Data</h3>
            <p>
              Aurora DSQL — a truly serverless Postgres with zero idle compute. Schema stays
              vanilla so the same migrations run locally in Docker and in production.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="arch-idx">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>API + reader</h3>
            <p>
              A Hono API on Lambda exposes the Google Reader–compatible surface and a
              first-party JSON API. A React reader lives on CloudFront. Your browser talks to
              Cognito; native clients use per-user API tokens.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Run your own reading flow.</h2>
      <p>The setup is a documented walkthrough — a few cloud resources and one pipeline.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-lg" href="/setup">read the setup guide</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 8rem) 0 clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }
  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 900px;
  }
  .hero .accent {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .lede {
    max-width: 640px;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .btn-lg {
    padding: 0.8rem 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .btn-ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--accent);
    border-color: var(--a-6);
  }
  .btn-ghost:hover {
    background: var(--a-6);
    color: #fff;
  }
  .hero-stats {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 3rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }
  .hero-stats li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .stat-num {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .features {
    background: var(--bg-elev);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .features h2 {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .card {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }
  .card .chip {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }
  .card p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .arch-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .arch-list li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .arch-idx {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    min-width: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 0.25rem;
  }
  .arch-list h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .arch-list p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .cta {
    text-align: center;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--accent-chip);
  }
  .cta p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    margin: 1rem 0 2rem;
  }
</style>